# Post-Processing & Real-Time Visual FX Engineering

This skill defines the mathematical models, shader algorithms, and pipeline steps for cinematic post-processing, tone mapping, lighting, and shadow systems.

---

## 1. Modern HDR Tone Mapping Algorithms

Tone mapping compresses High Dynamic Range (HDR) values ($[0, \infty)$) into displayable Standard Dynamic Range (SDR) ($[0, 1]$).

### A. ACES Filmic Tone Mapping (Fitted Narkowicz Formula)
```hlsl
// High-efficiency ACES approximation
float3 ACESFilm(float3 x) {
    float a = 2.51f;
    float b = 0.03f;
    float c = 2.43f;
    float d = 0.59f;
    float e = 0.14f;
    return saturate((x * (a * x + b)) / (x * (c * x + d) + e));
}
```

### B. AgX Tone Mapping (Modern Blender / Next-Gen Standard)
* Superior color preservation in high-luminance highlights (prevents saturated fire/explosions from collapsing into harsh yellow/magenta).
* Preserves perceived contrast across wide dynamic ranges.

