## 2. Progressive Dual-Filtering Bloom Pipeline

Traditional single-pass Gaussian blur requires huge kernel sizes that cripple GPU memory bandwidth.
* **Modern Progressive Pipeline (Call of Duty / Unreal Engine):**
  1. **Threshold & Prefilter:** Extract bright pixels above threshold ($L > 1.0$), with a soft knee curve to prevent harsh pixelated stepping.
  2. **Downsample Chain (5–6 Mip Levels):** Downsample sequentially ($1/2 \rightarrow 1/4 \rightarrow 1/8 \rightarrow 1/16 \rightarrow 1/32$), sampling 13 bilinear taps per pass to eliminate temporal flickering.
  3. **Upsample & Composite Chain:** Progressively upsample with a 9-tap tent filter, adding the previous mip level:
     $$\text{Mip}_{k-1}^{\text{accum}} = \text{Upsample}(\text{Mip}_k^{\text{accum}}) + \text{Mip}_{k-1}$$
  4. **Tone Mapping Injection:** Blend final bloom into main scene before tone mapping.

