## 3. Cascaded Shadow Maps (CSM) Splits

For open-world environments, split the camera frustum into 3 to 4 cascades to balance shadow resolution:
* **Logarithmic / Practical Split Formula:**
  $$C_i = \lambda \cdot \left( z_{\text{near}} \left( \frac{z_{\text{far}}}{z_{\text{near}}} \right)^{\frac{i}{m}} \right) + (1 - \lambda) \cdot \left( z_{\text{near}} + \frac{i}{m} (z_{\text{far}} - z_{\text{near}}) \right)$$
  Where $m = \text{cascade count}$, $\lambda \in [0.5, 0.9]$ blends logarithmic and uniform distribution.
* **Texel Snapping:** Snap orthographic light projection matrices to shadow map texel increments to completely eliminate shadow edge shimmering during camera movement:
  $$\text{offset} = \text{round}\left( \frac{\text{lightPos}}{\text{texelSize}} \right) \times \text{texelSize}$$
